  message: "FIXED and merged (dev 25f51b3fc5, carried forward). The gate now skips only when\nthe manifest's SELECTED_TESTS section is empty, which is the question it always\nmeant to ask; changed-source files continue to size the coverage target, which\nlegitimately needs them.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE: tests/test_ci_pytest_selection_gate.py executes the\nextracted shell block rather than reading it, and asserts pytest was invoked for\nthe exact manifest shape that exposed the bug (0 changed source files, 1\nselected test). Mutation-tested: reintroducing the source-keyed condition turns\n3 of the 4 original tests red.\n\nCORROBORATING, and stated as corroboration rather than proof: both PRs merged\nsince carried \"Changed source files: 0\" with a non-empty selection - precisely\nthe shape that used to skip - and both ran their suites in CI.\n\nRELATED, filed separately rather than folded in: WI-vilor is a SECOND fail-open\nhole in this same block (a git error reading as \"nothing changed\", plus a diff\nbase that no longer exists after a rebase merge). Same family, different\nquestion - this item is about which question the gate asks, WI-vilor about what\nit does when it cannot get an answer."  # a222
